U6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-08T02:41:55Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:42:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.8.dev3 [51105ccbe] (and previous snapshots), 4.7.stable, 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL ES 3/ANGLE (Compatibility) - ANGLE (AMD, AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (0x00001681) Direct3D11 vs_5_0 ps_5_0, D3D11-32.0.21043.19003) - AMD Ryzen 7 7735HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 13.69 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nFrom time to time, the rendered frames will jitter (or appear to slowdown/stutter).\nI'm using a 60hz screen and if lock the framerate to 60 it shows the issue clearly.\n\nEnabling VSync solves the issue, and it makes no difference if physics interpolation is active (nor if movement is happening on _process or _physics_process).\n\nThis only happens when using OpenGL ANGLE, as switching to OpenGL (Non-ANGLE) or Forward+ fixes the issue.\n\nAs far as i could tell, ANGLE does not tear the image, so it ends up with some weird pacing.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-Make sure OpenGL ANGLE is set as rendering driver.\n-Run project.\n-Go fullscreen.\n-Might need to change the max FPS if using different refresh rate than 60hz.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[cam-jitter-demo.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31934073/cam-jitter-demo.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123296/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}